# ── machine-local, not part of the site ──────────────────────────────────
# There is no package.json here and there must never be one (see CLAUDE.md),
# so a lockfile can only be the residue of a stray `npm install` or of running
# tools/make-icons.mjs. Ignored rather than committed, because committing it
# would be the first half of exactly the version carrier this repo refuses to
# grow.
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# read/config.js is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. read/index.html loads it with a
# <script src>, so a missing file is a 404 in every reader's console on every
# page load. The committed copy declares nothing -- empty apiUrl, empty key --
# which is the honest state while the server half does not exist, and a deploy
# overwrites it with the real per-deployment values. Neither of those is a
# secret; they are kept out of git so this public repo is not tied to one
# project and rotating a key is not a code change. See the file's own header.
